<title>MEXICO: Ece up on racecouse concession - traders.</title>
<headline>Ece up on racecouse concession - traders.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares listed by restaurant chain Ece Corp chalked up strong gains on the Mexican bourse in midday trading on Monday after news it had jointly won bidding for a concession to run Mexico City's racecourse, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;They'll be doing good business, the market really welcomed the news and it is among the most traded stocks,&quot; a desk trader said.</p>
<p>Ece nominal shares were up 60 centavos at 11.32 pesos.  </p>
<p>Mexico's Interior Ministry announced Friday night it had ruled in favor of a bid tendered by Ece Corp and Maxxam Inc to run horseracing at Mexico City's &quot;Americas&quot; racecourse.</p>
<p>(( --Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9562))</p>
